\alttext(Rejected loops/cycles retain the count, accepted edges lower it, and the final forest retains two components.)

> Checking selected work without hiding sorting

The trace counts two root searches per scanned edge and partitions scans into
accepted edges plus cycle rejections. It excludes path-halving steps,
validation, sorting, allocations, copying and time. The standard whole-algorithm
bound is O(n+M log(M+1)) with O(n+M) runtime storage; union-find adds
near-linear amortized work. Selected counters alone are not a timing estimate.

For each n below, supply n negative loops, n−1 increasing chain edges and one
heavy closing edge. Exactly2n input records are validated/sorted, but scanning
stops after2n−1: the heavy final cycle is never visited. The actual counts check
these formulas, rather than plotting theoretical curves as measured work.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kruskal_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| n | input edges | actual scans | actual accepted | actual rejected | actual find calls | " "twice actual scans |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {16, 64, 256, 1024, 4096}) {
        std::vector<dm::algorithms::WeightedEdge> e;
        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < n; ++i)
            e.emplace_back(i, i, -1);
        for (std::size_t i = 1; i < n; ++i)
            e.emplace_back(i - 1, i, double(i));
        e.emplace_back(0, n - 1, 1e6);
        const auto a = dm::algorithms::kruskal_work(n, e);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n,
                   a.work.input_edges, a.work.scanned_edges,
                   a.work.accepted_edges, a.work.cycle_rejections,
                   a.work.find_calls, 2 * a.work.scanned_edges);
        x.push_back(std::log2(n));
        y.push_back(std::log2(a.work.find_calls));
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "actual", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, y, "", {37, 99, 235}, 4).title("Actual root-search calls on controlled inputs").x_label("log2(n)").y_label("log2(actual root-search calls)").save_svg("build/kruskal_work.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| n | input edges | actual scans | actual accepted | actual rejected | actual find calls | twice actual scans |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 16 | 32 | 31 | 15 | 16 | 62 | 62 |
| 64 | 128 | 127 | 63 | 64 | 254 | 254 |
| 256 | 512 | 511 | 255 | 256 | 1022 | 1022 |
| 1024 | 2048 | 2047 | 1023 | 1024 | 4094 | 4094 |
| 4096 | 8192 | 8191 | 4095 | 4096 | 16382 | 16382 |
\image(figures/kruskal_work.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual scan/root-search counts on inputs with an unvisited heavy tail.)
\alttext(Every computed find count equals twice actual scans; all supplied edges still contribute to sorting and validation.)

> Scope and verification

All endpoints must be in[0,n), all weights finite, and every accepted-edge
sequential sum must remain finite. Empty/singleton graphs count as connected and
return a zero total. Scalar/work calls retain no optional history. Trace mode
owns original edge records, actual scan decisions and outcome; its million-entry
quota counts complete M input edges plus actual scanned records, admitted before
copying/scanning. Zero disables only that quota, whose record count excludes
output/runtime storage, capacities and bytes/RAM. This report reuses the
existing canonical Kruskal API; no second implementation is introduced.

Independent Prim-style minimum-forest calculations checked101 weighted graphs
and238 actual scans, including original root-component membership, stable edge
order, acceptance and early termination. Native complete spanning-subset
enumeration certifies the original unique total20, with explicit
disconnected/tie/parallel/loop controls and selected-work identities. Existing
canonical Kruskal and Euclidean-MST trace/certificate tests also passed; no
duplicate core implementation was introduced. The ten-report shared build
passed141 native CTest cases,45 directly instrumented
address/undefined-behaviour sanitizer cases,90 compiled/executed public
examples,412/412 scoped file definitions plus11/11 changed lagged-Fibonacci
engine definitions, and ten representative clangd hovers. All four complete
report programs executed and all four native figures were visually reviewed.
Receipts and repeatable checks are retained under
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-184-193/`.

> References

J. B. Kruskal, Jr.(1956),
[On the shortest spanning subtree of a graph and the traveling salesman problem|https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9939-1956-0078686-7],
Proceedings of the American Mathematical Society7(1),48–50. Stable ties,
disconnected forests and finite signed weights are explicit native contracts
beyond the original distinct-positive-weight setting.
